{
  "info": {
    "name": "Fuel Route Optimizer",
    "description": "Worked examples for the fuel route optimizer API. Set the collection variable base_url if the service is not on http://127.0.0.1:8000.\n\nRun the requests top to bottom. The coast to coast example forces twenty fuel stops, and running it twice in a row demonstrates the cache: the second call reports external_api_calls 0 and returns in single digit milliseconds.\n\nEvery 200 body carries map_url, an absolute link to the browser map for the same trip, and request.start and request.finish each carry snapped_to_road_miles, how far the routing provider moved the point to reach a road. and every stop carries leg_miles, the distance driven since the previous stop. The route line is thinned by default; request 3b asks for the provider's full geometry and shows the two vertex counts.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "1. Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/health",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "health"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Confirms the service is up and reports how many stations are loaded and when the dataset was generated."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "2. Seattle to Miami (coast to coast, several stops)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('exactly one external routing call', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(body.performance.external_api_calls).to.eql(1));",
              "pm.test('multiple fuel stops', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(body.fuel_plan.stop_count).to.be.above(4));",
              "pm.test('no leg exceeds the tank range', () => {",
              "    const stops = body.fuel_plan.stops;",
              "    const range = body.request.range_miles;",
              "    let previous = 0;",
              "    stops.forEach((stop) => {",
              "        pm.expect(stop.offset_miles - previous).to.be.at.most(range + 0.5);",
              "        previous = stop.offset_miles;",
              "    });",
              "    pm.expect(body.route.distance_miles - previous).to.be.at.most(range + 0.5);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('gallons match distance at the stated mpg', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(body.fuel_plan.total_gallons * body.request.mpg)",
              "      .to.be.closeTo(body.route.distance_miles, 0.5));",
              "pm.test('map_url is an absolute link to /map', () =>\n    pm.expect(body.map_url).to.match(/^https?:\\/\\/.+\\/map\\?/));",
              "pm.test('leg_miles sums to the distance', () => {\n    const legs = body.fuel_plan.stops.reduce((a, s) => a + s.leg_miles, 0);\n    const last = body.fuel_plan.stops[body.fuel_plan.stops.length - 1].offset_miles;\n    pm.expect(legs + (body.route.distance_miles - last)).to.be.closeTo(body.route.distance_miles, 0.5);\n});",
              "pm.test('route line is thinned by default', () =>\n    pm.expect(body.route.geometry_vertices).to.be.below(body.route.source_vertices));",
              "pm.test('endpoints were not moved to reach a road', () => {\n    pm.expect(body.request.start.snapped_to_road_miles).to.be.below(5);\n    pm.expect(body.request.finish.snapped_to_road_miles).to.be.below(5);\n});",
              "console.log('stops', body.fuel_plan.stop_count,",
              "            'cost $' + body.fuel_plan.total_cost_usd,",
              "            'total_ms', body.performance.total_ms);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Seattle, WA&finish=Miami, FL",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Seattle, WA"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "Miami, FL"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "About 3,300 miles, so a 500 mile tank forces at least seven fill ups. Seattle has stations within the origin radius, so origin_price_source reports the cheapest station near the origin."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3. Seattle to Miami again (cache hit)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('served from cache', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(body.performance.cache).to.eql('hit'));",
              "pm.test('no external call at all', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(body.performance.external_api_calls).to.eql(0));",
              "console.log('cached total_ms', body.performance.total_ms);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Seattle, WA&finish=Miami, FL",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Seattle, WA"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "Miami, FL"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "The identical request a second time. The plan is memoised, so this makes no external call and returns in single digit milliseconds."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "3b. Seattle to Miami with geometry=full (same plan, every vertex)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('full geometry returns every provider vertex', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(body.route.geometry_vertices).to.eql(body.route.source_vertices));",
              "pm.test('the plan is unchanged by the geometry choice', () =>",
              "    pm.expect(body.fuel_plan.total_cost_usd).to.eql(1026.29));",
              "console.log('vertices', body.route.geometry_vertices, 'body bytes', pm.response.responseSize);"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Seattle, WA&finish=Miami, FL&geometry=full",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Seattle, WA"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "Miami, FL"
            },
            {
              "key": "geometry",
              "value": "full"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "The same trip asking for the provider's own 35,438 vertices instead of the 3,396 the default keeps. Compare the response size with request 2: the plan, the stops and the cost are identical, only the line is heavier."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "4. Los Angeles to New York (origin with no nearby station)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Los Angeles, CA&finish=New York, NY",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Los Angeles, CA"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "New York, NY"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "About 2,800 miles. The price file carries no truck stop within 25 miles of Los Angeles, so origin_price_source reports that the departure price came from the nearest station along the route instead. The assumptions block in the response says so explicitly."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "5. Chicago to Houston (mid length)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Chicago, IL&finish=Houston, TX",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Chicago, IL"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "Houston, TX"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "About 1,090 miles through dense truck stop country, so the optimiser has plenty of choice."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "6. Coordinates instead of place names",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=39.7392,-104.9903&finish=39.0997,-94.5786",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "39.7392,-104.9903"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "39.0997,-94.5786"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Denver to Kansas City given as raw coordinates. Both forms resolve locally with no geocoding call."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "6b. Bare city names (population dominance)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Denver&finish=Chicago",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Denver"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "Chicago"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "No state given. Denver resolves to Colorado because it outweighs the Denvers in Iowa, North Carolina and Pennsylvania by more than ten to one in population. Try start=Springfield to see the 400 that names the states when no namesake dominates."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "7. Tuned parameters (small tank, wide corridor)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Denver, CO&finish=Chicago, IL&range_miles=250&mpg=6.5&corridor_miles=25",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Denver, CO"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "Chicago, IL"
            },
            {
              "key": "range_miles",
              "value": "250"
            },
            {
              "key": "mpg",
              "value": "6.5"
            },
            {
              "key": "corridor_miles",
              "value": "25"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "A loaded truck rather than the default vehicle: half the range and 6.5 mpg, which roughly doubles the number of stops and the cost."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "8. Error: unknown place (400)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('400 with a readable error', () => {",
              "    pm.response.to.have.status(400);",
              "    pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.property('error');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Nowhereville, ZZ&finish=Miami, FL",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Nowhereville, ZZ"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "Miami, FL"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "An unresolvable place returns 400 with a message naming the input, never a stack trace."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "9. Error: invalid parameter (400)",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/route-plan?start=Denver, CO&finish=Chicago, IL&mpg=0",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "v1",
            "route-plan"
          ],
          "query": [
            {
              "key": "start",
              "value": "Denver, CO"
            },
            {
              "key": "finish",
              "value": "Chicago, IL"
            },
            {
              "key": "mpg",
              "value": "0"
            }
          ]
        },
        "description": "Zero mpg is rejected by validation with a field level detail."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ]
}
